\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh's¦112263 messenger¦112261 went from¦112264 Gilgal¦112266 to¦112267 Bokim¦112269 and¦112271 told¦112271 \add the Israelis\add*, “I brought¦112272 you all out of¦112282 Egypt¦112274 and¦112275 led you here to¦112277 this land¦112279 that¦112280 I promised¦112281 to¦112282 your ancestors¦112282. I had said¦112283 that I wouldn't ever break¦112286 my¦112287 agreement¦112287 with¦112288 you all,
\v 2 but¦112291 that¦112298 you mustn't form treaties¦112295 with¦112304 the¦112296 peoples who lived¦112296 here, rather you must¦112300 tear¦112300 down¦112300 their¦112299 altars¦112299. But¦112291 you all haven't obeyed¦112303 what¦112305 I said. What¦112305 have¦112308 you \add gone and\add* done¦112308?\x + \xo 2:2: \xt Exo 34:12-13; Deu 7:2-5.\x*
