\v 6 Then all¦116504 of¦116504 the¦116506 \add prominent\add* citizens¦116506 of¦116506 Shekem and¦116508 all¦116508 of Beyt¦116510-Millo¦116511 assembled¦116503 themselves, and¦116512 they¦116512 went¦116512 and¦116513 installed Abimelek¦116516 as king¦116517 beside an oak tree¦116520 near¦116518 the¦116520 standing pillar\f + \fr 9:6 \ft Likely connected with idol worship.\f* that¦116521 was¦116523 in¦116523 Shekem.
\s1 Yotam's tree parable
\rem /s1 Jotham's Parable; The Parable of the Trees
\p
\v 7 \add ≈When¦116525\add* they told¦116525 Yotam¦116526, he¦116527 went¦116527 and¦116528 stood¦116528 on¦116529 the¦116529 top¦116529 of¦116529 Mt¦116530. Gerizim¦116532 and shouted¦116535 out to¦116537 them¦116537 all \add ≈in¦116529 a loud voice¦116534\add*, “Listen¦116538 to¦116539 me¦116539, citizens¦116540 of¦116540 Shekem¦116541, so¦116542 God¦116544 will listen¦116542 to¦116543 all of you.
\v 8 Once the¦116548 trees¦116548 went¦116547 about in order¦116552 to appoint a king¦116551 for themselves¦116550, \add ≈So\add* they¦116552 said¦116552 to¦116553 the \em olive¦116553 tree¦116553\em*, ‘Reign¦116554 over¦116556 us¦116556.’
