\v 10 Then¦119555 his¦119556 father¦119556 went \add ≈to¦119557 visit\add* the¦119559 woman¦119559, and¦119560 \add ≈in the custom of the young¦119567 men¦119567\add* \add of the time\add*, Shimshon¦119562 \add ≈held\add* a party \add there\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈When¦119571\add* they saw¦119570 him¦119571, they¦119572 brought¦119572 thirty¦119573 close¦119574 friends¦119574 to join him¦119576.\f + \fr 14:11 \ft Although we can understand the words here, we're not certain of the implications, or perhaps the cultural traditions. Did Shimshon appear too alone? Too intimidating? Or was it just bringing more friends for good food and drink?\f*
