\v 3 Shimshon¦119828 \add ≈responded¦119826\add*, “This¦119830 time¦119830 I'm blameless concerning the¦119831 Philistines¦119831 when I¦119835 \add ≈cause¦119834 trouble¦119837 for¦119827\add* them¦119836.”
\v 4 Then¦119839 \add *he¦119839\add* went¦119839 and¦119841 captured¦119841 three¦119842 hundred¦119844 foxes¦119845 and \add ≈tied them in¦119860 pairs\add*—tail to¦119850 tail. He¦119840 took¦119846 torches¦119847, and \add ≈tied\add* one¦119855 torch¦119854 between¦119856 \add ≈the¦119858 tails¦119859 of¦119858 each pair\add*.
\v 5 He¦119862 \add ≈lit\add* the torches¦119865 and let \add @the¦119862 foxes¦119862\add* loose into the¦119867 grain¦119867 \add ≈crops\add* of¦119867 the¦119868 Philistines¦119868. As a result, he¦119862 burnt¦119869 both the¦119873 standing¦119873 grain \add plants\add* and also¦119866 the¦119870 \add harvested\add* \add #stacks¦119870\add* of¦119870 sheaves¦119870, and even a vineyard¦119876 and an olive¦119877 orchard.
