\p “Shimshon,” they \add ≈replied¦119879\add*, “the¦119886 son-in-law¦119886 of¦119886 the¦119887 \add ≈man from Timnah\add*, because¦119888 he¦119889 took¦119889 \add @Shimshon's¦119885\add* wife¦119892 and¦119893 gave¦119893 her¦119893 to¦119894 his¦119894 close¦119894 friend¦119894.” As a result, the¦119896 Philistines went¦119895 \add to Timnah\add* and¦119897 they¦119897 burnt¦119897 \add both\add* \add @the¦119892 woman¦119892\add* and¦119895 her¦119898 father¦119901.
\v 7 Then¦119904 Shimshon¦119906 told¦119904 them¦119905, “Since you actually did¦119909 that¦119910 \add horrible thing\add*, I¦119917 certainly \add ≈won't\add* stop¦119917 until I've¦119914 avenged¦119914 myself¦119914 against you all.”
\v 8 Then¦119919 he¦119919 attacked¦119919 the¦119929 Philistines and¦119919 \add ≈crippled¦119920 many¦119920 of¦119920 them¦119920, before¦119920 going¦119920 to¦119920\add* Etam's¦119931 rock¦119930 where he lived¦119928 in¦119929 a cave.
\s1 Shimshon defeats the Philistines
\rem /s1 Samson Defeats the Philistines
\p
\v 9 \add ≈However\add*, the¦119935 Philistine \add warriors\add* went¦119934 and¦119936 camped¦119936 in¦119937 Yehudah¦119937, and¦119938 spread¦119938 out¦119938 \add around the town of\add* Lehi¦119939.
