\v 14 \add ≈When they'd taken him\add* as far as Lehi¦120040, the¦120041 Philistines¦120041 shouted¦120045 \add triumphantly\add* \add ≈when they saw¦120046\add* him. Then Yahweh's¦120050 spirit¦120049 \add ≈rose in¦120060\add* \add @Shimshon¦120035\add* and¦120047 the ropes¦120052 \add ≈around\add* his¦120056 arms¦120056 \add ≈just seemed as weak as burnt¦120059\add* flax¦120057 stalks \add ≈when he¦120035 simply snapped them off¦120061 him\add*.
\v 15 He¦120066 saw¦120066 a fresh¦120070 donkey's¦120069 jawbone¦120067 \add lying on the ground\add*, and¦120071 he¦120071 reached¦120071 out¦120071 his¦120072 hand¦120072 and¦120073 \add ≈grabbed¦120073\add* it¦120073, and¦120074 he¦120074 slaughtered a thousand¦120077 \add Philistine\add* men¦120078 with¦120076 it¦120076.
