\p
\v 4 \add ≈Sometime\add* after¦120243 that, \add @Shimshon¦120246\add* fell in love¦120246 with¦120248 a \add Philistine\add* woman¦120247 named¦120250 Delilah¦120251 who \add lived in\add* the¦120248 Sorek¦120249 valley¦120248.
\v 5 The¦120255 Philistine leaders¦120255 came¦120253 to her¦120258 and \add ≈requested\add*, “Make him open up. \add ≈Find out what makes him strong¦120263, and how¦120262 we¦120266 can beat\add* him¦120267, so that we¦120268 can tie¦120268 him up \add ≈to keep him in¦120262 our power¦120263\add*. Then¦120253 we'll¦120268 each¦120274 give¦120271 you one¦120275 thousand¦120275 one¦120276 hundred¦120276 silver¦120277 coins.”
